The rule in recover_json_object says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one." For the input fence[ A B ] C, the fence holds A and B, so the last object inside the fence is B; k_recovery returns B. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] C, the fence holds only A, so the last object inside the fence is A; k_recovery returns A. Therefore the check's answer moves from B to A.